      "repair_reason": "- No automated repair is needed; the remaining action is ordinary maintainer landing after current-head gates and compatibility-risk acceptance.; Cleared: The diff narrows an availability-sensitive MCP transport path and does not add dependencies, secret handling, workflow execution, or supply-chain changes. (sha=8240e5782a23296014d91bea7700774ca403af34)",
      "review_summary": "The PR changes MCP HTTP fetch response normalization to stop reading body-less foreign response text bodies, adds focused MCP OAuth tests, and adds an Unreleased changelog entry.\n\nPR surface: Source -2, Tests +27, Docs +1. Total +26 across 3 files.\n\nReproducibility: yes. source-reproducible: current main reaches `await response.text()` for a body-less non-204/205/304 MCP response, and the existing compatibility test exercises that text-only foreign-response shape. I did not run a live repro in this read-only review.",
